}
```
For the `components` option, these strings determine which JSX elements (**always including** `` thru ``) should be checked for having content. This is a good use case when you have a wrapper component that simply renders an `h1` element (like in React):
```js
// Header.js
const Header = props => {
  return (
    <h1 {...props}>{ props.children }</h1>
